          "title": "Creational Patterns: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Idea",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Decouple ==what gets created== from the code that asks",
                "Callers depend on an **interface**, not a concrete class"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Five Patterns",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Pattern",
                "Core question",
                "Idea"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Singleton",
                  "==How many?==",
                  "One instance"
                ],
                [
                  "Factory Method",
                  "==Which class?==",
                  "Subclass picks the type"
                ],
                [
                  "Abstract Factory",
                  "==Which family?==",
                  "Related objects together"
                ],
                [
                  "Builder",
                  "==How to assemble?==",
                  "Step-by-step construction"
                ],
                [
                  "Prototype",
                  "==Copy from what?==",
                  "Clone; costly to create, cheap to copy"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Spot the Need",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`new ConcreteClass()` scattered around",
                "Constructors with many parameters",
                "Switch on a type tag"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Rule of thumb",
              "text": "Start with a plain constructor. Refactor to a pattern only when the ==variation actually appears==."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why use a creational pattern?** Callers depend on an interface, not a class",
                "**Many optional parameters?** Builder",
                "**Which question does Abstract Factory answer?** Which family?",
                "**When to refactor to a pattern?** When the variation appears"
              ],
