    {
      "title": "Singleton and Factory Method",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Singleton and Factory Method",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Singleton",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Exactly one instance== plus a global access point",
                "Private constructor, static field, static `getInstance()`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Thread Safety and Pitfalls",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Init",
                "Thread-safe?"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Lazy, no lock",
                  "{red:No}: two threads can both create"
                ],
                [
                  "Lazy + lock",
                  "{green:Yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "Double-checked + `volatile`",
                  "{green:Yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "Eager static initializer",
                  "{green:Yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "Enum singleton",
                  "{green:Yes}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Hidden ==global state==",
                "Hard to unit test: cannot swap in a mock",
                "Breaks with one per tenant or per process"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Prefer",
              "text": "Dependency injection with a ==single shared instance==, not `getInstance()` calls everywhere."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Factory Method",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Creator",
                    "sub": "calls create()",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Subclass",
                    "sub": "overrides create()",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Product",
                    "sub": "concrete type",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Base class declares `create()`; ==subclasses== choose the concrete product",
                "Use when the class is unknown until ==runtime== or a framework lets users plug in products"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A subclass per product explodes the class count; use a ==static factory== if no extension is needed"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Abstract Factory and Builder",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Abstract Factory and Builder",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Abstract Factory",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "One interface, ==one create method per product==: `createButton()`, `createCheckbox()`",
                "Each concrete factory returns a ==matching set==: DarkThemeFactory, LightThemeFactory",
                "Use when products belong together and are {red:never mixed} across families",
                "Typical cases: UI themes, cross-platform widgets, per-database DAOs"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Factory",
                "createButton()",
                "createCheckbox()"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "DarkThemeFactory",
                  "DarkButton",
                  "DarkCheckbox"
                ],
                [
                  "LightThemeFactory",
                  "LightButton",
                  "LightCheckbox"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Pitfall",
              "text": "==Easy to add families, costly to add products==: a new product type changes the interface and every concrete factory."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Builder",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Separate ==construction== of a complex object from its representation",
                "Chained calls end in `build()`, which returns an ==immutable== result",
                "Cures the ==telescoping constructor==: many optional parameters"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "Pizza p = new Pizza.Builder()",
                "    .size(L)",
                "    .cheese()",
                "    .build();  // validates, then freezes"
              ],
              "note": "chain the options, build() last"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`build()` must ==validate== required fields, or you get half-built objects",
                "Overkill for objects with two or three fields: use a plain constructor"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Prototype and Choosing Between Patterns",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
