    {
      "title": "Common Mistakes with Creational Patterns",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Common Mistakes with Creational Patterns",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Singleton Misuse",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Used as a convenient ==global==: hides dependencies, tests become order-dependent",
                "Fix: **inject** the one shared instance",
                "Lazy init without a lock: two threads can both create it"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "private static volatile Db inst;",
                "static Db get() {",
                "  if (inst == null) synchronized (Db.class) {",
                "    if (inst == null) inst = new Db();",
                "  }",
                "  return inst;",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "double-checked locking"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Over-Engineering",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Factory or Builder on a simple object: extra ==indirection==, no variation to justify it"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Copy and Build Bugs",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Prototype pays off when an object is ==costly to create== but cheap to copy"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Mistake",
                "Symptom",
                "Fix"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Shallow clone with mutable lists",
                  "Editing the clone changes the original",
                  "**Deep copy** nested fields"
                ],
                [
                  "`build()` skips validation",
                  "Half-built object fails far from the cause",
                  "Validate required fields in `build()`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Remember",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Rule of thumb",
              "text": "Add a pattern only when ==variation== appears. Inject singletons, deep-copy clones, validate in `build()`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Creational Patterns Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Creational Patterns Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Which Pattern",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Pattern",
                "Asks",
                "Pick when"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Singleton",
                  "How many?",
                  "Need exactly one"
                ],
                [
                  "Factory Method",
                  "Which class?",
                  "Class unknown until runtime"
                ],
                [
                  "Abstract Factory",
                  "Which family?",
                  "Matched families"
                ],
                [
                  "Builder",
                  "How to assemble?",
                  "Many optional params"
                ],
                [
                  "Prototype",
                  "Copy from what?",
                  "Costly to create; clone instead"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Must-Know Facts",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Singleton==: private constructor + static `getInstance()`",
                "Thread-safe: {green:enum} or eager init; inject, don't go global",
                "==Factory Method==: subclass overrides `create()`, returns one product",
                "==Abstract Factory==: one interface, a product family; easy to add families, hard to add products",
                "==Builder==: stepwise, final `build()` validates; often immutable",
                "==Prototype==: `clone()` an object; pick shallow or deep first"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Pitfalls",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Lazy singleton without a lock: two instances",
                "Builder without validation in `build()`: half-built objects"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Shallow vs deep",
              "text": "Mutating a ==shallow== clone changes the original; **deep-copy** mutable fields."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A lazy Singleton does `if (inst == null) inst = new Config();`. Two threads call getInstance() first, at the same time. What can go wrong?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Both see `null`, so ==two instances== get created.",
                "Fix: eager init, an enum singleton, or a lock with a `volatile` field."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "You clone an Order whose `items` list is shared (shallow copy), then add an item to the clone. What does the original hold?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "The ==new item too==: both objects point to one list.",
                "Deep-copy mutable nested fields."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "You add createSlider() to an Abstract Factory that already has DarkThemeFactory and LightThemeFactory. What breaks?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Every concrete factory must implement it.",
                "Adding ==products== is costly; adding families is easy."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
